<title>POLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS POOL B RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS POOL B RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>KATOWICE, Poland 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of world</p>
<p>championship pool B ice hockey matches on Wednesday:</p>
<p> Switzerland    2    Kazakhstan   5   (2-3 0-1 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Switzerland - Claudio Micheli 4, Gian-Marco Crameri 19</p>
<p>Kazakhstan - Maxim Komisarov 11, Andrey Raiskiy 14, Andrey</p>
<p>Pchelyakov 14, Andrey Zaliypyatsckih 37, Yerlan Samgymbayev</p>
<p>58.</p>
<p>    Denmark	   1    Britain	9   (1-1 0-5 0-3)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Denmark - Ronny Struve Larsen 7.</p>
<p>Britain - Paul Leonhard Adey 21, 45, 57, Steven Moria 2, 32,</p>
<p>Michael Bishop 32, Richard Little 39, Graham Garden 39, Timothy</p>
<p>Cranston 58.</p>
<p>    Poland	    4     Austria     6     (1-1 3-1 0-4)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Poland - Slawomir Wieloch 3, Janusz Hajnos 21, Marek</p>
<p>Koszowski 34, Miroslaw Tomasik 38</p>
<p>Austria - Richard Nasheim 55, 60, Christoph Brandner 15,</p>
<p>Thomas Searle 33, Martin Ulrich 49, Gerhard Unterluggauer 53</p>
